    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "that makes sense. i'll try to focus more on the lifting motion and the bevel angle. one more thing—is there any way to tell if the grain is working against me before i make the cut? like, are there specific visual cues in the wood that suggest a high risk of the grain tearing or splintering once i start the paring process?",
